-- ============================================================
-- Marksmanship: Piercing Shots
-- ============================================================
--
-- TODO.md: "Critical Aimed, Steady and Chimera Shots bleed the target for 30%
--  of the damage dealt over 8 sec and have a 33/66/100% chance to reset the
--  duration of Lacerating Shot on your target, and increase the duration of
--  Lacerating Shot by 2/4/6 sec (3 ranks)"
--
-- The bleed half already works on this core and is left alone: core's
-- spell_hun_piercing_shots (spell_hunter.cpp:1622) reads aurEff->GetAmount()
-- and feeds CastDelayedSpellWithPeriodicAmount, so flattening 10/20/30% to a
-- flat 30% is one column -- EffectBasePoints1 29 on all three ranks.  63468 is
-- already 8s with 1s ticks; no change there either.
--
-- The refresh half is a second AuraScript on the same spell ids.  See the
-- spell_proc block below for the constraint that shapes it, and for the
-- Chance = 100 that stops this change quietly nerfing the bleed.
--
-- The duration half is Effect2, a plain SPELLMOD_DURATION, and it is the same
-- shape as Lethal Instincts extending Instinctive Fire: a spellmod applies to
-- every application of Lacerating Shot, including casts that never proc this
-- talent, which is what the script path cannot do.  Base points 1999/3999/5999
-- because a flat modifier's value is BasePoints + max(1, DieSides), and
-- $/1000;s2 renders that same total as 2 / 4 / 6.
--
-- NOTE THIS IS A DAMAGE INCREASE, not just uptime.  Lacerating Shot is
-- DurationIndex 1 (10000 ms) with EffectAmplitude1 2000, so it ticks 5 times;
-- an aura's tick count is its max duration divided by the amplitude, computed
-- at creation.  +2/4/6 sec therefore buys 6/7/8 ticks, and because the per-tick
-- amount is a fixed 3.6% of ranged attack power, total bleed damage rises
-- 20/40/60%.  Chosen deliberately gentler than Lethal Instincts' +50/100%, and
-- the whole knob is EffectBasePoints2 on three rows if it wants retuning.
--
-- The refresh and the extension compose correctly: Aura::RefreshDuration resets
-- to GetMaxDuration(), which already includes the modifier because
-- Aura::CalcMaxDuration (SpellAuras.cpp:806) applied it when the aura was made.
--
-- One cosmetic limit: Lacerating Shot's own description says "over $d", and $d
-- is resolved client-side from the base DurationIndex.  The client cannot know
-- about a server-side spellmod, so that line keeps reading 10 sec.  The tooltip
-- is per-tick ("every $t1 seconds") and stays accurate.



